5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,We need to see what actually happened to past projects. I’m looking into post-occupancy review ratings and survey findings in the older blocks.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I’m examining the timetable records on rooms out of service and the decade of delivery schedules by project rationale.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m checking tender records over three budget cycles and weather days in the site diaries.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I’m looking into renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier and bench technicians' weekly manual routines.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I’m reviewing staffing posts since the hiring freeze and booking data for specialist and general rooms.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, do you think the weather delays will affect the new plan’s timeline?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, weather only hits exposed work. I’m tracking how long rooms stay out of service, not the rain.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, rain is just one variable. I’m watching how tender prices drift against the index, which is where the real budget risk hides.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that makes sense. I’m checking if we ever set aside money to replace old gear, because the bills keep arriving.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the technicians’ hours are tied to the equipment you’re checking. I’m seeing if the staffing gap matches their workload.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, your delivery schedule data is key. I want to know if the projects that actually worked were the ones that stayed on time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, the data shows inspection-driven works stayed on schedule, while comfort-based ones slipped. I’m checking if that pattern predicts our current options.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, that’s a useful distinction. I’m seeing if the tender drift matches those delays, or if the costs are just rising regardless of the schedule.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, if the technicians are stuck on manual checks, does that mean the equipment is failing us? I’m worried the costs are hidden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, it’s not just failing; it’s a staffing mismatch. I’m checking if we can redeploy those spare technician hours to cover the unfilled posts.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, if comfort projects slip, does that mean we should only pick plans with hard safety mandates?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, not necessarily. I’m checking if the delay pattern holds for our specific candidates, not just generalizing from past inspection-driven works.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, I’m watching the tender drift. If the costs are rising regardless of the schedule, we need to know if the budget can absorb that shock.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, if we can shift those spare hours, maybe we stop paying for extra help. I’m hoping the numbers show a way out.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, shifting hours is a stopgap, not a fix. I’m checking if the booking data shows we actually need more staff or just better allocation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
